      "text": "%spark.ipyspark\n\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n\ndef migrate_pdf_between_azure_containers(\n    source_storage_account_name,\n    source_container_name,\n    source_blob_name,\n    destination_storage_account_name,\n    destination_container_name,\n    destination_blob_name,\n    storage_account_key\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Migrate a PDF file from one Azure Blob container to another using Apache Spark.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    source_storage_account_name : str\n        The name of the source Azure Storage account\n    source_container_name : str\n        The name of the source container\n    source_blob_name : str\n        The name/path of the source PDF blob\n    destination_storage_account_name : str\n        The name of the destination Azure Storage account\n    destination_container_name : str\n        The name of the destination container\n    destination_blob_name : str\n        The name/path for the destination PDF blob\n    storage_account_key : str\n        The access key for the Azure Storage accounts (assuming same key for both accounts)\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a Spark session\n    spark \u003d SparkSession.builder \\\n        .appName(\"PDF Migration Between Azure Blob Containers\") \\\n        .config(\"spark.hadoop.fs.azure.account.key.{}.blob.core.windows.net\".format(source_storage_account_name), \n                storage_account_key) \\\n        .config(\"spark.hadoop.fs.azure.account.key.{}.blob.core.windows.net\".format(destination_storage_account_name), \n                storage_account_key) \\\n        .getOrCreate()\n    \n    # Define the source and destination paths\n    source_path \u003d f\"wasbs://{source_container_name}@{source_storage_account_name}.blob.core.windows.net/{source_blob_name}\"\n    destination_path \u003d f\"wasbs://{destination_container_name}@{destination_storage_account_name}.blob.core.windows.net/{destination_blob_name}\"\n    \n    print(f\"Starting migration of PDF file from {source_path} to {destination_path}\")\n    \n    try:\n        # Read the PDF as a binary file using Spark\u0027s binary file format\n        pdf_df \u003d spark.read.format(\"binaryFile\").load(source_path)\n        \n        # Write the PDF to the destination\n        pdf_df.write.format(\"binaryFile\").save(destination_path, mode\u003d\"overwrite\")\n        \n        print(f\"Successfully migrated PDF from {source_path} to {destination_path}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error during migration: {str(e)}\")\n    finally:\n        # Stop the Spark session\n        spark.stop()\n\nif __name__ \u003d\u003d \"__main__\":\n    # Replace these with your actual Azure Storage details\n    SOURCE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT \u003d \"lightningdata\"\n    SOURCE_CONTAINER \u003d \"datalake\"\n    SOURCE_BLOB_NAME \u003d \"wesfarmers_annual_report_2024.pdf\"\n    \n    DESTINATION_STORAGE_ACCOUNT \u003d \"lightningdata\"\n    DESTINATION_CONTAINER \u003d \"knowledgebase\"\n    DESTINATION_BLOB_NAME \u003d \"wesfarmers_annual_report_2024.pdf\"\n    \n    STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY \u003d \"JvCD+5XrNzXV9gPE7DPYFGLxPLDKGqwMCbEuhH9U4RR1dKuwML5d/IHwS9GJQ92Q3TfW//gb0lq4+ASt7x+ytg\u003d\u003d\"\n    \n    # Execute the migration\n    migrate_pdf_between_azure_containers(\n        SOURCE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT,\n        SOURCE_CONTAINER,\n        SOURCE_BLOB_NAME,\n        DESTINATION_STORAGE_ACCOUNT,\n        DESTINATION_CONTAINER,\n        DESTINATION_BLOB_NAME,\n        STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY\n    )\n",
